AB  - In this paper, we prove propagation of s 1-Gevrey regularity (s \in (0, 1)) and analyticity (s = 1) for the Vlasov--Navier--Stokes system on Td \times Rd (and Rd \times Rd) using a Fourier space method in analogy to the results proved for the Euler system in [I. Kukavica and V. Vicol, Proc. Amer. Math. Soc., 137 (2009), pp. 669--677] and [C. D. Levermore and M. Oliver, J. Differential Equations, 133 (1997), pp. 321--339] and for Vlasov-Poisson system in [R. Velozo Ruiz, Ann. Inst. H. Poincare\' C Anal. Non Lin\'eaire, 38 (2021), pp. 1145--1165]. More precisely, we give quantitative estimates for the growth of the s1-Gevrey norm and decay of the regularity radius for the solution of the system in terms of V x u, the spatial density \rhof, and the diameter of the support in the velocity variable of the distribution of particles f. In particular, this implies existence of s 1-Gevrey (s \in (0, 1)) and analytic (s = 1) solutions for the Vlasov--Navier--Stokes system in Td \times Rd (and Rd \times Rd), and global Gevrey solutions in T3 \times R3 for sufficiently small data, and an initial datum for the Vlasov equation with compact support in velocity.
